cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite both the software and the paper."
title: "Metacognitive Profile Atlas"
authors:
  - family-names: Cacioli
    given-names: Jon-Paul
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0000-7054-2014
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Melbourne, Australia"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/synthiumjp/metacognitive-profile-atlas"
abstract: >
  A domain-stratified benchmark for LLM metacognitive monitoring.
  1,500 MMLU items, 33 frontier LLMs, 46,157 scored observations
  (version 2: unparsed answers and parser-imputed confidences
  excluded). Type-2 AUROC per model-domain cell with bootstrap 95%
  CIs and error counts. Companion to Cacioli (2026), arXiv:2605.06673v2.
keywords:
  - large-language-models
  - metacognition
  - confidence-calibration
  - benchmarks
  - psychometrics
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "The Metacognitive Profile Atlas: Domain-level confidence discrimination in 33 frontier LLMs on MMLU"
  authors:
